## Modeling the Four Seasons

Seasons are a fixed set of four possibilities. Each has associated data: weather, months, and what comes next.

### The Season Enum

```xiom
enum Season {
  Spring,
  Summer,
  Autumn,
  Winter,
}
```

### Weather Descriptions

```xiom
fn Season.weather(self) -> Str {
  match self {
    Spring => { return "Warm and rainy"; }
    Summer => { return "Hot and sunny"; }
    Autumn => { return "Cool and windy"; }
    Winter => { return "Cold and snowy"; }
  }
}
```

### Getting the Next Season

Match on the current season to return the next one in the cycle:

```xiom
fn Season.next(self) -> Season {
  match self {
    Spring => { return Season.Summer; }
    Summer => { return Season.Autumn; }
    Autumn => { return Season.Winter; }
    Winter => { return Season.Spring; }
  }
}
```

### Season Months

```xiom
fn Season.months(self) -> Str {
  match self {
    Spring => { return "March - May"; }
    Summer => { return "June - August"; }
    Autumn => { return "September - November"; }
    Winter => { return "December - February"; }
  }
}
```

### Using Season Methods

```xiom
let current = Season.Summer;
current.weather();     // "Hot and sunny"
current.next();        // Season.Autumn
current.next().next(); // Season.Winter
```

### Cycling Through an Entire Year

```xiom
var s = Season.Spring;
s = s.next();  // Summer
s = s.next();  // Autumn
s = s.next();  // Winter
s = s.next();  // Spring (wraps around)
```

